            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns the effective date of a veteran\u2019s disability compensation award."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Adolfo Arellano",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a9cac9ed25211c81fcf5c3177664d3950957e1148870844a198bbc3e3099e105",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a9cac9ed2521-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner Adolfo Arellano argued that the award\u2019s effective date should be governed by \u00a75110(b)(1), which makes the effective date the day after discharge if the application is filed within one year."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Secretary of Veterans Affairs",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a9cac9ed25211c81fcf5c3177664d3950957e1148870844a198bbc3e3099e105",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a9cac9ed2521-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Secretary of Veterans Affairs argued that \u00a75110(b)(1) is not a statute of limitations and that any presumption of equitable tolling is rebutted by the statutory text and structure."
      }
    ],
