            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts announced the case: \u201cWe\u2019ll hear argument next in Case 21\u2011432, Arellano versus McDonough.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson asked whether the issue was a statute of limitations and whether equitable tolling applied."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson further asked whether the agency would apply the statute as written and then refer the matter to the Veterans Court for equitable tolling."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0010"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked what other deadlines the parties thought were at issue."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0011"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked whether practical problems and congressional intent made equitable tolling implausible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether the statute required filing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan questioned the Irwin presumption, noting that the first point made by counsel was that it does not apply at all."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "James R. Barney",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner counsel James R. Barney argued that the subsections the Secretary points to do not relate to service\u2011connected disability compensation, the focus of \u00a75110(b)(1)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "James R. Barney",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to James R. Barney, barney further argued that the Secretary\u2019s reliance on equitable exceptions elsewhere actually strengthens the presumption of equitable tolling for \u00a75110(b)(1)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court noted that most deadlines in civil litigation are tollable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5f4a9108d72de0004c92014799b2f4462994644b4ee0024d91618ba69951a88f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5f4a9108d72d-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court also observed that there has not been a floodgate problem with people seeking equitable tolling in the nation\u2019s courts."
      }
    ],
